WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:04.320
The next optimization in view mode I want to talk about

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.879
is Quad Overdraw.

3
00:00:05.879 --> 00:00:10.039
Now, Quad Overdraw is used to help determine areas

4
00:00:10.039 --> 00:00:15.060
which are going to cause your GPU to go in to overdrive

5
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.719
trying to calculate triangles.

6
00:00:16.719 --> 00:00:19.079
Now, the reason for this is that GPUs work on a 2

7
00:00:19.079 --> 00:00:21.480
by 2 quad granularity, which

8
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.960
means that small thin triangles that

9
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:28.320
are smaller than 2 by 2 pixels result in extra work

10
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.469
for the GPU to have to do.

11
00:00:31.469 --> 00:00:34.929
Quad Overdraws will show you which meshes could

12
00:00:34.929 --> 00:00:38.850
be suffering from this issue and allow

13
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.369
you to make better, more informed choices about how

14
00:00:41.369 --> 00:00:42.450
to approach that.

15
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.490
Now, the cool thing about Quad Overdraw

16
00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.429
is that the easiest way to address this

17
00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:50.369
is to simply add a level of detail

18
00:00:50.369 --> 00:00:54.689
and then reduce the level of detail's geometry

19
00:00:54.689 --> 00:00:57.630
so that you can still have mesh

20
00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.929
that has a silhouette that is similar while being cheaper

21
00:01:00.929 --> 00:01:01.710
to render.

22
00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.950
One other thing to note about Quad Overdraw

23
00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.209
is that if you're working on a VR project,

24
00:01:06.209 --> 00:01:09.310
Quad Overdraw is particularly important to have

25
00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:12.590
to pay attention to because, remember, VR is rendering not

26
00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:15.269
everything just once but everything twice.

27
00:01:15.269 --> 00:01:17.230
So any way that we can cut down

28
00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:20.909
on the amount of work or overwork the GPU has to do

29
00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:25.299
will be a big win for optimization overall.

30
00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:29.150
As with all of our other view modes,

31
00:01:29.209 --> 00:01:36.069
we want to try to keep the view in the ideal to moderate.

32
00:01:36.069 --> 00:01:38.950
And again, the idea here is to look

33
00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:43.909
for areas that have issues and not try and overoptimize

34
00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:49.430
to make our entire scene completely blue or green,

35
00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.870
destroying the artwork in a negative way.
